    "text": "{\n  \"anomaly_detected\": true,\n  \"confidence\": 0.5,\n  \"anomalies\": [\n    {\n      \"category\": \"short_to_ground\",\n      \"components\": [\"IC1\", \"C12\", \"C13\", \"J4\"],\n      \"pins\": [\"IC1.A2\", \"IC1.A1\", \"C12.1\"],\n      \"nets\": [\"BAT+\", \"GND\"],\n      \"observed\": \"On EthernetAndPower, the MODE pin (A1) wire runs to a vertical wire at about x=783 that continues down to the bottom GND bus at y\u2248608. The VIN pin (A2) wire, which comes from the BAT+ junction at x\u2248698, also meets that same vertical line at x\u2248783. If the two wires join there, the battery/input rail (BAT+) is tied directly to the GND bus, which also carries C12's ground end, C13 and IC1 GND. The junction is not clearly marked, so this depends on whether the wires actually connect.\",\n      \"expected\": \"MODE (A1) should go to GND only. VIN (A2) should connect to BAT+ only and must not share a node with GND. The 2.2 \u00b5F input cap C12 should sit between BAT+ and GND, not in a short.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"`VIN` (pins A2/B2) \u2192 `BAT+`.\"},\n        {\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"`MODE` (pin A1) \u2192 `GND`\"},\n        {\"source\": \"schematic\", \"quote\": \"EthernetAndPower sheet: IC1 FAN53610AUC33X pins MODE (A1), VIN (A2); vertical wire at x\u2248783 from MODE junction down to the GND bus at y\u2248608\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"If VIN is shorted to GND, the battery feed is shorted through the regulator input, which would drain or damage the 18650 cell and prevent the 3.3 V rail from coming up.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.5\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The EthernetAndPower sheet appears to route the FAN53610 MODE pin and the VIN pin onto a single vertical wire that reaches the GND bus, which would short BAT+ to GND. The junction is hard to confirm from the drawing, so confidence is moderate. The rest of the power, EPD and keyboard connectivity matches the specification.\